      children: "Third, extract complex logic into custom hooks immediately. If your component has more than 50 lines of logic that isn't directly related to rendering, it belongs in a hook. This makes the logic testable in isolation, reusable across components, and easier to understand. Teams that follow this pattern religiously end up with components that are 30-50 lines of mostly JSX, backed by hooks that handle all the complexity. React Query, SWR, and Apollo Client have proven this pattern works at massive scale-they're essentially collections of hooks with thin component wrappers."
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
