    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Fifth, test controlled and uncontrolled modes, accessibility, and edge cases explicitly. These aren't nice-to-haves-they're the difference between a component that works in demos and one that works in production. Every reusable component should have tests verifying: both controlled and uncontrolled behavior, keyboard navigation, screen reader compatibility, what happens when optional callbacks are undefined, and rapid state changes. This testing strategy is used by every component library at companies like Shopify, Atlassian, and Microsoft."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h2, {
